112	Color isn't about "what looks nice" — it's about what the design FEELS.
113	
114	**Building a Palette**:
115	
116	```css
117	/* Dark, Confident, Premium */
118	:root {
119	  --bg-primary: #0a0a0a;
120	  --bg-secondary: #171717;
121	  --bg-tertiary: #262626;
122	  --text-primary: #fafafa;
123	  --text-secondary: #a3a3a3;
124	  --accent: #22c55e;  /* Confident green */
125	  --accent-subtle: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.1);
126	}
127	
128	/* Light, Warm, Approachable */
129	:root {
130	  --bg-primary: #fffbf5;
131	  --bg-secondary: #fff7ed;
132	  --bg-tertiary: #ffedd5;
133	  --text-primary: #1c1917;
134	  --text-secondary: #78716c;
135	  --accent: #ea580c;  /* Warm orange */
136	  --accent-subtle: rgba(234, 88, 12, 0.1);
137	}
138	
139	/* High Contrast, Editorial */
140	:root {
141	  --bg-primary: #ffffff;
142	  --bg-secondary: #f5f5f5;
143	  --text-primary: #000000;
144	  --text-secondary: #525252;
145	  --accent: #dc2626;  /* Bold red */
146	  --accent-subtle: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.05);
147	}
148	```
149	
150	**The 60-30-10 Rule**:
151	- 60% dominant (background)
152	- 30% secondary (cards, sections)
153	- 10% accent (CTAs, highlights)
154	
155	### Motion as Narrative
156	
157	Animation tells a story. What's your story?
158	
159	**Page Load Orchestration**:
160	```css
161	/* Hero elements enter in sequence */
162	.hero-badge {
163	  animation: fadeSlideUp 0.6s ease-out 0.1s both;
164	}
165	.hero-title {
166	  animation: fadeSlideUp 0.6s ease-out 0.2s both;
167	}
168	.hero-subtitle {
169	  animation: fadeSlideUp 0.6s ease-out 0.3s both;
170	}
171	.hero-cta {
172	  animation: fadeSlideUp 0.6s ease-out 0.4s both;
173	}
174	
175	@keyframes fadeSlideUp {
176	  from {
177	    opacity: 0;
178	    transform: translateY(20px);
179	  }
180	  to {
181	    opacity: 1;
182	    transform: translateY(0);
183	  }
184	}
185	```
186	
187	**Scroll-Triggered Reveals**:
188	```javascript
189	// Intersection Observer for scroll animations
190	const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
191	  entries.forEach(entry => {
192	    if (entry.isIntersecting) {
193	      entry.target.classList.add('animate-in');
194	    }
195	  });
196	}, { threshold: 0.1 });
197	
198	document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
199	```
200	
201	**Hover States That Surprise**:
202	```css
203	.card {
204	  transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
205	}
206	
207	.card:hover {
208	  transform: translateY(-4px);
209	  box-shadow: 
210	    0 20px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1),
211	    0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
212	}
213	
214	/* Or more dramatic */
215	.card:hover {
216	  transform: scale(1.02) rotate(-0.5deg);
217	}
218	```
219	
220	### Backgrounds as Atmosphere
221	
222	The background sets the mood before any content is read.
223	
224	**Gradient Mesh**:
225	```css
226	.gradient-mesh {
227	  background: 
228	    radial-gradient(at 40% 20%, hsla(28, 100%, 74%, 0.3) 0px, transparent 50%),
229	    radial-gradient(at 80% 0%, hsla(189, 100%, 56%, 0.2) 0px, transparent 50%),
230	    radial-gradient(at 0% 50%, hsla(355, 100%, 93%, 0.3) 0px, transparent 50%),
231	    radial-gradient(at 80% 50%, hsla(340, 100%, 76%, 0.2) 0px, transparent 50%),
232	    radial-gradient(at 0% 100%, hsla(269, 100%, 77%, 0.3) 0px, transparent 50%);
233	}
234	```
235	
236	**Noise Texture**:
237	```css
238	.noise::before {
239	  content: '';
240	  position: fixed;
241	  top: 0;
242	  left: 0;
243	  width: 100%;
244	  height: 100%;
245	  background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 400 400' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noiseFilter'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='4' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noiseFilter)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E");
246	  opacity: 0.03;
247	  pointer-events: none;
248	  z-index: 1000;
249	}
250	```
251	
252	**Dot Pattern**:
253	```css
254	.dots {
255	  background-image: radial-gradient(circle, #333 1px, transparent 1px);
256	  background-size: 20px 20px;
257	}
258	```
259	
260	**Glassmorphism**:
261	```css
262	.glass {
263	  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
264	  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
265	  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
266	  box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
267	}
268	```
269	
270	---
271	
272	## Design Decision Framework
273	
274	When stuck, ask these questions:
275	
276	1. **What's the ONE thing?** — If users remember one element, what is it?
277	2. **Would I screenshot this?** — Is there a moment worth sharing?
278	3. **Does it feel designed?** — Or does it feel generated?
279	4. **What's the emotion?** — Confident? Playful? Serious? Luxurious?
280	5. **Is it brave?** — Did I play it safe or commit to a direction?
281	
282	---
283	
284	## Anti-Pattern Detection
285	
286	Before shipping, scan for these:
287	
288	| Anti-Pattern | Fix |
289	|--------------|-----|
290	| Inter font | Replace with distinctive alternative |
291	| Purple gradient | Choose contextual palette |
292	| All centered | Add asymmetry or left-align |
293	| No animations | Add orchestrated page load |
294	| Solid background | Add texture, gradient, or pattern |
295	| Evenly spaced colors | Apply 60-30-10 rule |
296	| Generic cards | Add unique styling treatment |
297	| Default shadows | Use layered, atmospheric shadows |
298	
299	---
300	
301	*Remember: Claude is capable of extraordinary creative work. Don't hold back.*
302

results.content:
1	# Mobile-First Patterns
2	
3	Comprehensive responsive CSS patterns learned from real-world implementation failures.
4	
5	## Hero Sections
6	
7	### Problem
8	2-column grid layouts leave empty space when one column is hidden on mobile.
9	
10	### Solution
11	Switch from `display: grid` to `display: flex` on mobile.
12	
13	```css
14	/* Desktop: 2-column grid */
15	.hero {
16	  display: grid;
17	  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
18	  gap: 64px;
19	  align-items: center;
20	  padding: 80px 0;
21	}
22	
23	/* Mobile: Centered flex */
24	@media (max-width: 768px) {
25	  .hero {
26	    display: flex;
27	    flex-direction: column;
28	    align-items: center;
29	    text-align: center;
30	    padding: 40px 20px;
31	    gap: 24px;
32	  }
33	
34	  .hero-content {
35	    align-items: center;
36	  }
37	
38	  .hero-badge {
39	    align-self: center;
40	  }
41	
42	  .hero-title {
43	    font-size: 32px;
44	    text-align: center;
45	  }
46	
47	  .hero-subtitle {
48	    font-size: 14px;
49	    text-align: center;
50	  }
51	
52	  .hero-cta {
53	    flex-direction: column;
54	    align-items: center;
55	    width: 100%;
56	  }
57	
58	  .hero-cta .btn {
59	    width: 100%;
60	    max-width: 280px;
61	  }
62	
63	  .hero-visual {
64	    display: none;
65	  }
66	}
67	```
68	
69	**Key Rule**: Grid reserves space for hidden columns. Flex doesn't.
70	
71	---
72	
73	## Large Selection Lists
74	
75	### Problem
76	Horizontal scroll for 20+ items is unusable on mobile — text gets cut off.
77	
78	### Solution
79	Collapsible accordion with category headers.
80	
81	```tsx
82	function MobileSelector({ categories }) {
83	  const [expanded, setExpanded] = useState<string | null>(null);
84	
85	  return (
86	    <div className="selector">
87	      {categories.map(cat => (
88	        <div 
89	          key={cat.name} 
90	          className={cn("category", expanded === cat.name && "expanded")}
91	        >
92	          <button
93	            className="category-header"
94	            onClick={() => setExpanded(
95	              expanded === cat.name ? null : cat.name
96	            )}
97	          >
98	            <span>{cat.name}</span>
99	            <ChevronDown className={cn(
100	              "transition-transform",
101	              expanded === cat.name && "rotate-180"
102	            )} />
103	          </button>
104	          
105	          <div className="category-items">
106	            {cat.items.map(item => (
107	              <button key={item.id} className="item">
108	                {item.name}
109	              </button>
110	            ))}
111	          </div>
112	        </div>
113	      ))}
114	    </div>
115	  );
116	}
117	```
118	
119	```css
120	.category-items {
121	  display: flex;
122	  flex-wrap: wrap;
123	  gap: 8px;
124	}
125	
126	@media (max-width: 768px) {
127	  .category-items {
128	    display: none;
129	  }
130	
131	  .category.expanded .category-items {
132	    display: flex;
133	    flex-direction: column;
134	    padding: 12px;
135	    background: var(--bg-secondary);
136	    border-radius: 8px;
137	  }
138	}
139	```
140	
141	---
142	
143	## Form Layouts
144	
145	### Problem
146	Multi-column form layouts get cut off on mobile.
147	
148	### Solution
149	Stack vertically with full width.
150	
151	```css
152	.form-row {
153	  display: flex;
154	  gap: 16px;
155	}
156	
157	.form-group {
158	  flex: 1;
159	}
160	
161	@media (max-width: 768px) {
162	  .form-row {
163	    flex-direction: column;
164	  }
165	
166	  .form-group {
167	    width: 100%;
168	  }
169	  
170	  .form-row.half-width {
171	    /* Even "half width" fields go full on mobile */
172	    flex-direction: column;
173	  }
174	}
175	```
176	
177	---
178	
179	## Status/Alert Cards
180	
181	### Problem
182	Inconsistent text alignment when stacking horizontal elements vertically.
183	
184	### Solution
185	Both `align-items: center` AND `text-align: center`.
186	
187	```css
188	.alert {
189	  display: flex;
190	  align-items: flex-start;
191	  gap: 12px;
192	  padding: 16px;
193	  border-radius: 8px;
194	}
195	
196	.alert-icon {
197	  flex-shrink: 0;
198	}
199	
200	.alert-content {
201	  flex: 1;
202	}
203	
204	@media (max-width: 768px) {
205	  .alert {
206	    flex-direction: column;
207	    align-items: center;  /* Center flex items */
208	    text-align: center;   /* Center text within items */
209	    gap: 8px;
210	  }
211	
212	  .alert-content {
213	    text-align: center;  /* Explicit for nested elements */
214	  }
215	
216	  .alert strong {
217	    text-align: center;  /* Block elements need explicit */
218	  }
219	}
220	```
221	
222	**Key Rule**: Stacked flex items need BOTH `align-items: center` AND `text-align: center`.
223	
224	---
225	
226	## Grid Layouts
227	
228	### Universal Mobile Collapse
229	
230	```css
231	.pricing-grid,
232	.feature-grid,
233	.team-grid,
234	.stats-grid,
235	.testimonial-grid {
236	  display: grid;
237	  gap: 24px;
238	}
239	
240	/* Desktop configurations */
241	.pricing-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
242	.feature-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
243	.team-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
244	.stats-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
245	.testimonial-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
246	
247	/* Tablet */
248	@media (max-width: 1024px) {
249	  .team-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
250	  .stats-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
251	}
252	
253	/* Mobile: Everything single column */
254	@media (max-width: 768px) {
255	  .pricing-grid,
256	  .feature-grid,
257	  .team-grid,
258	  .stats-grid,
259	  .testimonial-grid {
260	    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
261	  }
262	}
263	```
264	
265	---
266	
267	## Navigation
268	
269	### Mobile Menu Pattern
270	
271	```tsx
272	function MobileNav() {
273	  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
274	
275	  return (
276	    <>
277	      {/* Mobile menu button */}
278	      <button 
279	        className="md:hidden"
280	        onClick={() => setOpen(!open)}
281	      >
282	        {open ? <X /> : <Menu />}
283	      </button>
284	
285	      {/* Mobile menu overlay */}
286	      <div className={cn(
287	        "fixed inset-0 bg-black/50 md:hidden transition-opacity",
288	        open ? "opacity-100" : "opacity-0 pointer-events-none"
289	      )} onClick={() => setOpen(false)} />
290	
291	      {/* Mobile menu panel */}
292	      <nav className={cn(
293	        "fixed top-0 right-0 h-full w-64 bg-background p-6",
294	        "transform transition-transform md:hidden",
295	        open ? "translate-x-0" : "translate-x-full"
296	      )}>
297	        {/* Nav items */}
298	      </nav>
299	    </>
300	  );
301	}
302	```
303	
304	---
305	
306	## Form Element Consistency
307	
308	### Always Style as a Group
309	
310	```css
311	/* WRONG - Only targets input */
312	.input {
313	  border: 2px solid var(--border);
314	  border-radius: 8px;
315	}
316	
317	/* CORRECT - All form fields */
318	.input,
319	.select,
320	.textarea {
321	  border: 2px solid var(--border);
322	  border-radius: 8px;
323	  padding: 12px 16px;
324	  font-size: 16px; /* Prevents iOS zoom */
325	  background: var(--bg-secondary);
326	  color: var(--text-primary);
327	}
328	```
329	
330	### Textarea Border Radius Exception
331	
332	Pill-shaped inputs look wrong on textareas:
333	
334	```css
335	.input,
336	.select {
337	  border-radius: 100px; /* Pill shape */
338	}
339	
340	.textarea {
341	  border-radius: 16px; /* Softer, but not pill */
342	}
343	```
344	
345	### Dropdown Option Styling
346	
347	`<option>` elements can't inherit backdrop-filter:
348	
349	```css
350	.select {
351	  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
352	  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
353	  color: white;
354	}
355	
356	/* Options need solid backgrounds */
357	.select option {
358	  background: #1a1a2e;
359	  color: white;
360	}
361	```
362	
363	### Prevent iOS Zoom on Focus
364	
365	iOS zooms on inputs with font-size < 16px:
366	
367	```css
368	input, select, textarea {
369	  font-size: 16px; /* Minimum to prevent zoom */
370	}
371	
372	/* Or use transform trick */
373	@media (max-width: 768px) {
374	  input, select, textarea {
375	    font-size: 16px;
376	  }
377	}
378	```
379	
380	---
381	
382	## Color Contrast Checklist
383	
384	### Badge/Pill Elements
385	
386	```css
387	/* WRONG - May be invisible */
388	.badge {
389	  background: var(--accent);
390	  color: white; /* Might not contrast */
391	}
392	
393	/* CORRECT - Ensure contrast */
394	.badge {
395	  background: var(--accent);
396	  color: var(--accent-foreground); /* Defined to contrast */
397	}
398	```
399	
400	### Color Swatches
401	
402	Swatches showing colors need visible borders:
403	
404	```css
405	.color-swatch {
406	  border: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
407	  box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
408	}
409	```
410	
411	### Dark Theme Form Labels
412	
413	```css
414	/* WRONG - Hardcoded */
415	.label {
416	  color: white;
417	}
418	
419	/* CORRECT - Semantic variable */
420	.label {
421	  color: var(--text-primary);
422	}
423	```
424	
425	---
426	
427	## Breakpoint Reference
428	
429	```css
430	/* Large Desktop */
431	@media (min-width: 1440px) {
432	  .container { max-width: 1280px; }
433	}
434	
435	/* Desktop */
436	@media (max-width: 1200px) {
437	  /* Stack sidebars, maintain content width */
438	}
439	
440	/* Tablet */
441	@media (max-width: 1024px) {
442	  /* Reduce grid columns */
443	}
444	
445	/* Mobile */
446	@media (max-width: 768px) {
447	  /* Full single-column, centered content */
448	}
449	
450	/* Small Mobile */
451	@media (max-width: 480px) {
452	  /* Compact spacing, reduced font sizes */
453	}
454	```
455	
456	---
457	
458	## Mobile Font Scaling
459	
460	```css
461	/* Base (desktop) */
462	.display { font-size: 64px; }
463	.h1 { font-size: 48px; }
464	.h2 { font-size: 36px; }
465	.h3 { font-size: 24px; }
466	.body { font-size: 16px; }
467	.small { font-size: 14px; }
468	
469	/* Mobile */
470	@media (max-width: 768px) {
471	  .display { font-size: 40px; }
472	  .h1 { font-size: 32px; }
473	  .h2 { font-size: 24px; }
474	  .h3 { font-size: 20px; }
475	  .body { font-size: 16px; } /* Keep readable */
476	  .small { font-size: 13px; }
477	}
478	```
479	
480	---
481	
482	## Touch Target Sizes
483	
484	Minimum 44x44px for touch targets (Apple HIG):
485	
486	```css
487	.btn,
488	.nav-link,
489	.icon-btn {
490	  min-height: 44px;
491	  min-width: 44px;
492	}
493	
494	@media (max-width: 768px) {
495	  .btn {
496	    padding: 14px 24px; /* Larger touch area */
497	  }
498	}
499	```
500	
501	---
502	
503	## Pre-Implementation Checklist
504	
505	Before finalizing any mobile design:
506	
507	- [ ] Hero centers on mobile (not left-aligned with empty space)
508	- [ ] All form fields (input, select, textarea) styled consistently
509	- [ ] Radio/checkboxes visible (especially transparent-border styles)
510	- [ ] Dropdown options have readable backgrounds
511	- [ ] Labels use semantic color variables
512	- [ ] Status/alert cards center properly
513	- [ ] Large selection lists use accordion (not horizontal scroll)
514	- [ ] Grid layouts collapse to single column
515	- [ ] Badge/pill text contrasts with background
516	- [ ] Color swatches have visible borders
517	- [ ] Touch targets are 44x44px minimum
518	- [ ] Font sizes are 16px+ to prevent iOS zoom
519	- [ ] Navigation has mobile menu pattern
